{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group D of the [[2010 FIFA World Cup]]''' began on 13 June and ended on 23 June 2010.<ref>{{cite press release |title=Match Schedule 2010 FIFA World Cup South Africa |website=FIFA.com|publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/64/42/24/fifawc2010matchschedulefinalversion.pdf |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091228213032/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/64/42/24/fifawc2010matchschedulefinalversion.pdf |url-status=dead |archive-date=28 December 2009 |access-date=6 December 2009 }}</ref> The group consisted of [[Germany national football team|Germany]], [[Australia men's national soccer team|Australia]], [[Serbia national football team|Serbia]] and [[Ghana national football team|Ghana]]. Along with [[2010 FIFA World Cup Group G|Group G]], it was considered to be a [[group of death]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Germany face early test of mettle |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/standings/group=249726/analysis.html |access-date=20 April 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100417082223/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/standings/group%3D249726/analysis.html |archive-date=17 April 2010 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

