===Germany vs Serbia===
Germany striker [[Miroslav Klose]] was sent off in the first half, and Serbia went ahead shortly afterwards with a goal from winger [[Milan Jovanović (footballer, born 1981)|Milan Jovanović]].

In the 59th minute, Serbia centre-back [[Nemanja Vidić]] was booked for a handball in the penalty box, but the ensuing penalty kick from [[Lukas Podolski]] was saved by goalkeeper [[Vladimir Stojković]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Play-by-Play |url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/southafrica2010/matches/round=249722/match=300061470/playbyplay.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140427152606/http://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/southafrica2010/matches/round=249722/match=300061470/playbyplay.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=27 April 2014 |website=FIFA.com |publisher=FIFA |access-date=11 July 2014}}</ref>

This was Germany's first loss in the group stage of a World Cup since [[1986 FIFA World Cup Group E|the 1986 edition of the tournament]],<ref >{{Cite web |website=MLS Soccer |date=2010 |title=Serbia stun 10-man Germany, blow group open |url=https://www.mlssoccer.com/news/serbia-stun-10-man-germany-blow-group-open}}</ref> and their first penalty miss in a World Cup (excluding penalty shoot-outs) since 1974.<ref >{{Cite web |website=BBC Sport|last=Lyon |first=Sam |date=2010 |title=Germany 0-1 Serbia |url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/world_cup_2010/matches/match_21/default.stm}}</ref>

